Bundled fonts
-------------

egui-pop-core (crates/egui-pop-core/fonts, compiled in by its
`bundled-fonts` feature, on by default) carries Inter (Copyright 2020 The
Inter Project Authors) and JetBrains Mono NL (Copyright 2020 The
JetBrains Mono Project Authors), subset, each under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1 (the OFL.txt beside it), not under egui-pop's licences. Their
sources, versions and changes are in that folder's README.md.

Gallery fonts
-------------

The gallery (crates/egui-pop-gallery, not published) carries the other
candidate fonts for its "Font pairs" page in
crates/egui-pop-gallery/assets/fonts, each under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1 (the OFL.txt beside it), not under egui-pop's licences: Noto
Sans and Noto Sans Mono (Copyright 2022 The Noto Project Authors), IBM
Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono (Copyright 2017 IBM Corp., with Reserved Font
Name "Plex"). Their sources, versions and changes are in that folder's
README.md. No published crate includes them.

Toasts
------

egui-pop's toasts (crates/egui-pop-api/src/toasts.rs) take ideas from
egui-notify (https://github.com/ItsEthra/egui-notify), MIT, Copyright (c)
2022-2023 ItsEthra: the slide in and out from the corner's side with
appear, idle and disappear states and a cubic ease-out (src/toast.rs,
src/lib.rs), the time-left bar that stops under the pointer, the newest
toast nearest the edge and the shadow (src/lib.rs), and the corner as a
choice (src/anchor.rs). No code is copied; the shapes are close. Its
licence is the MIT licence below.

Editor-inspired themes
----------------------

egui-pop's editor-inspired themes (crates/egui-pop-tokens/themes) reuse
colour values from the following projects, under the MIT licence unless
stated otherwise. The theme names are used only to describe where the
colours come from; egui-pop is not affiliated with or endorsed by their
authors. "GitHub" is a trademark of GitHub, Inc.

- github-light, github-dark, github-light-high-contrast,
  github-dark-high-contrast: GitHub's VS Code theme
  (https://github.com/primer/github-vscode-theme), version 6.3.5,
  Copyright (c) 2020 Primer.
- catppuccin-latte, catppuccin-mocha: Catppuccin for VS Code and the
  Catppuccin palette (https://github.com/catppuccin/vscode,
  https://github.com/catppuccin/palette), version 3.19.0,
  Copyright (c) 2021 Catppuccin.
- one-light: Atom One Light for VS Code
  (https://github.com/akamud/vscode-theme-onelight), version 2.3.0,
  Copyright (c) 2015 Mahmoud Ali; after Atom's One Light (GitHub, MIT).
- one-dark-pro: One Dark Pro (https://github.com/Binaryify/OneDark-Pro),
  version 3.20.3, Copyright (c) 2013-2022 Binaryify; after Atom's One Dark
  (GitHub, MIT).
- solarized-light, solarized-dark: Solarized
  (https://github.com/altercation/solarized), Copyright (c) 2011 Ethan
  Schoonover; workbench mapping from Visual Studio Code's Solarized themes
  (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode), Copyright (c) 2015 - present
  Microsoft Corporation.
- gruvbox-light, gruvbox-dark: Gruvbox by Pavel Pertsev
  (https://github.com/morhetz/gruvbox), stated as MIT/X11 in its README
  (the repository has no licence file); workbench mapping from Gruvbox
  Theme for VS Code (https://github.com/jdinhify/vscode-theme-gruvbox),
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2017 JD.

Each theme file also records its source (repository, file, version,
commit, licence) under "$extensions" -> "org.egui-pop.source".

Rerun-like kits
---------------

The example kit examples/kits/rerun-like, dark and light (data only,
not in any published crate), reuses token values (colours, sizes, font sizes) from the design tokens of
the Rerun viewer's re_ui crate (https://github.com/rerun-io/rerun,
crates/ui_tools/re_ui: data/dark_theme.ron, data/light_theme.ron,
data/color_table.ron, src/design_tokens.rs), Copyright (c) Rerun
Technologies AB, under the MIT licence (below) or the Apache License 2.0.
No code is copied. The name is used only to say where the values come
from; egui-pop is not affiliated with or endorsed by Rerun Technologies
AB.

